    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283-a3">

                <pb facs="0404" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg298"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State to Consul-General
                        Rodgers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 160, of the 25th of May last, inclosing copy of a letter to be
                    addressed by the senior consul of the consular body at Shanghai to the dean of
                    the diplomatic corps at Peking, protesting against the restrictions threatened
                    by the Chinese on the natural growth of the foreign settlement at Shanghai
                    toward the north and east.</p>
                <p>This proposed letter has the approval of the department, and the American
                    minister at Peking will be instructed to support the request of the consular
                    body unless he sees some serious objection.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
